  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uyoma Food Security Cage Fishing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Uyoma Food Security Self Help Group Siaya County, Rarieda Sub-County, Agok Village Type of Project: Income Generating Activity (IGA) - Fish Farming Cages Project Description: Empower young female fishers through cage fish farming. Grant Requested: $10,000 to buy cage fish farming equipment, motorized boat engine, Fishing tanks, wire mesh, barbed wire, water proof cement, fish pellets, fish processing tables, ropes, floaters, and fish packaging materials Community/Group Contribution: Land, locally available materials, all the transport related to the project, labor, and security Project Manager: Churchill Otieno Koobetto Beneficiary: 52 members and their families and 269 school children - 133 male 188 female.</narrative>
  </description>
